-- title:
--   The shared reporting-bank extent fits its polynomial allocation envelope
-- statement:
--   For a natural input size $n$, put $m=\operatorname{log2}(n)$, $h=\lfloor\lfloor\sqrt[3]{m}\rfloor/2\rfloor$, $J=20\lfloor m/(200h)\rfloor$, and $M=2^{2048(m+1)}$. Here $\operatorname{log2}(0)=0$ and natural division by zero is zero.
--   Let $E(n)$ be the defined shared reporting-bank extent at parameters $(h,J,n)$, measured from base zero. This allocation bound includes the initial header and Pascal workspace, the metadata slab, and the level payload and construction workspace for every occurrence and every pair of source bands, using $n$ as a bound on each band count. Then
--   $$E(n)\le5000(M+1)^5(n+1)^2.$$
--
--   This bounds the entire shared reporting-bank allocation by the same finite polynomial envelope later used in its machine resource contract.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/c0ldzy17/three-sum-lean/blob/2b639655e07421b9ac743de9090459bab473a7c0/Submission/ThreeSum/SharedReportingBankResourceBoundsScales.lean#L173-L201

